So the escalation must keep its boolean-ish contract for failure vs return-the-sha on success:
- success + sha known → return sha (string).
- success + sha unknown (probe failed) → return... we must NOT throw. Return `true`? Then tracked returns true → refreshHeadSilent: pushedSha=true → truthy... headMoved(uHead, true) → false → no record. But we COULD fall back to the re-read in that case. So refreshHeadSilent should only trust the pushed sha when it's a real sha string:

