Hmm wait — the `if (released || <= 0)` branch is ALSO redundant then (Math.min(remaining, initial-reserved) when reserved<=0 → Math.min(remaining, initial) — hmm, not identical: remaining could be < initial (already spent) — Math.min picks remaining ✓; released same. So actually the whole function collapses to `Math.min(remaining, max(0, initial - reserved))`... when reserved=0: min(remaining, initial) = remaining since remaining ≤ initial always. So the if is provably redundant too — but the reviewer only flagged the merge-path branch; minimal change = remove only what was flagged. Keep the if (it documents intent + avoids computing when released). Minimal surgical edit.

